# What docker ships to the daemon as the build context, and what `COPY . .`
# then puts in the image. Without this file the context is the whole crate
# directory -- including target/, which is tens of gigabytes of host-built
# artifacts that then land on top of the image's own target/ and throw away
# every dependency the build stage just compiled. That is the difference
# between a one-minute rebuild and a ten-minute one.
target/
coverage/

# Credentials and certificates. Compose hands these to the container as
# secrets at run time; they have no business in an image layer.
keys/
secrets/
*.key
*.crt
*.csr
*.der

# Not part of the build.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.gcloudignore
.DS_Store
Dockerfile*
cloudbuild.yaml
**/*.md
profile.json.gz
